{
  "_comment": "Durable role/provenance map for corpus/samples/. Every sample directory is FLAT: the source page is source.<ext>, references are ref-<provenance>.<ext> (ref-unknown-<n>.<ext> where the provenance could not be recovered), outputs are export.<ext> / render.<ext> / project.zip, and project.zip is also unpacked to project/. This file records which original file plays which role, since the names no longer say. corpus/samples/<id>/meta.json is generated from it. Keys are sample ids; NSFW samples are keyed 'NSFW/sampleN' and carry sfw: false. NOTE: '(copy 1)' files were mangatranslate.com renders that collided with the source filename on download - they are references, not duplicates, and none were byte-identical to their namesake. On sample24 the roles are inverted (plain name = English). NSFW source lang is assumed 'ja' - it was never recorded and no NSFW page has been through a builder yet. 'parked' names directories under samples/ holding superseded versions of a page; they are ignored by --verify.",
  "provenance_vocabulary": [
    "human",
    "mangatranslator.ai",
    "mangatranslate.com",
    "mangatranslate.online",
    "google-lens",
    "local",
    "manually-edited",
    "unknown"
  ],
